WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:03.203
[wind rumbling]

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:06.172
OK, so Bobby,
where we're heading

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:09.275
is 100 foot drop off that lip.

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:13.413
We're right on the edge of
this, like, boulder, slab

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:16.216
of rock that just curls away.

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:17.984
And it's one of
these awkward ones,

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:20.587
because you can't
see over the lip.

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:23.256
We're going to go across
and try and secure ourselves

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:25.058
and then figure out a way down.

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:26.626
Let's follow this moss, OK?

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:27.894
All right.

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:30.930
It's getting steeper, and
it's actually a drop-off,

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:34.200
meaning if I were to take
two steps this way and slide,

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:37.036
I would fall off the edge of it.

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:39.072
It's super slick and scary.

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:40.707
BEAR GRYLLS: So
we're probably going

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:42.275
to need the rope for this.

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:43.209
Have you got that--

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:45.044
have you got that claw?

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:46.312
I don't know what that is.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.914
BEAR GRYLLS: Did you get that?

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:51.084
We're going to use these bear
claws-- they're called talons--

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.685
and dig it into the moss.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:55.221
The moss is only about
that deep, though, so this

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:56.990
is a little bit sketchy.

00:00:57.056 --> 00:00:58.792
So if you stand on those--

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.894
BOBBY BONES: That moss
will hold those claws?

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.331
Well, that
probably would hold.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:07.634
BOBBY BONES: Probably work.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.601
Yeah.

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:09.803
I'm a little nervous
about this one.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:10.703
I'm not going to lie to you.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.704
BEAR GRYLLS: OK.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:13.606
Let's get this rope sorted.

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:17.710
I think this is definitely
a baptism by fire--

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:20.079
or rather rain and wind--

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.414
for Bobby.

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:23.583
These sort of things,
in perfect conditions,

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:26.286
are all really manageable,
but everything becomes harder

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.321
when you can't feel
your fingers and you're

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:30.924
cold and wet through.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.492
Put your weight in it, Bobby.

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:34.360
Put your weight, because I need
your counterbalance on this.

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:35.228
That's it.
Keep going.

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:36.062
Keep coming.

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:38.331
Keep coming.

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:39.232
Keep your weight on it.

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:40.066
BOBBY BONES: OK.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.034
Lean back?

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:41.868
BEAR GRYLLS: Yeah.

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.703
All good.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.739
Now, those talons are
actually holding well.

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:50.076
[dramatic music]

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:51.344
Look at that.

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:53.146
There's long water
slide off to your head.

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:54.180
BOBBY BONES: Oh, my god.

00:01:58.084 --> 00:01:58.852
BEAR GRYLLS: OK.

00:01:58.918 --> 00:01:59.652
Here we go.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:02.755
Well done.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:03.790
Keep walking down.

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:05.959
Walk it down.

00:02:06.025 --> 00:02:06.960
That's it.

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.195
BOBBY BONES: Oh, god.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:10.196
Keep it going.

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:15.101
BEAR GRYLLS: Almost there.

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:16.069
Good, Bobby.

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:18.605
Good.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:20.974
BOBBY BONES: Whoo!

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.342
BEAR GRYLLS: Good job.

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:23.009
OK.

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:24.410
And that talon held.

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:25.945
Looking back, it was
definitely a smart decision

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.380
to use the rope on this.

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:28.848
So from here, we're pushing on.

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:31.751
And what I can see
is it is boggy.

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:33.086
Norway.

00:02:33.152 --> 00:02:34.153
Bogs.

